 to have received three Michelin stars. Located in the SoMa district, Benu was opened in 2010 by chef Corey Lee, the former Chef de Cuisine at the French Laundry."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-benu-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benu_(restaurant)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["New American cuisine","cuisine/new-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from New American cuisine","links":[["63 Clinton","dish/63-clinton"],["Boka (restaurant)","dish/boka-restaurant"],["Boulevard (restaurant)","dish/boulevard-restaurant"],["Cafe La Haye","dish/cafe-la-haye"],["Canlis","dish/canlis"],["Clinton Street Baking Company & Restaurant","dish/clinton-street-baking-company-restaurant"],["Elements (restaurant)","dish/elements-restaurant"],["Four Seasons Restaurant","dish/four-seasons-restaurant"],["Gotham Bar and Grill","dish/gotham-bar-and-grill"],["Gramercy Tavern","dish/gramercy-tavern"],["Harvest Moon Cafe","dish/harvest-moon-cafe"],["King's Carriage House","dish/king-s-carriage-house"],["Laurelhurst Market","dish/laurelhurst-market"],["Montrio Bistro","dish/montrio-bistro"],["Moody Tongue","dish/moody-tongue"],["Peacock Inn (Princeton, New Jersey)","dish/peacock-inn-princeton-new-jersey"],["Rich Table","dish/rich-table"],["Saison (restaurant)","dish/saison-restaurant"],["Somni","dish/somni"],["Sons & Daughters (restaurant)","dish/sons-daughters-restaurant"],["State Bird Provisions","dish/state-bird-provisions"],["The Musket Room","dish/the-musket-room"],["Union Square Cafe","dish/union-square-cafe"],["Woodberry Kitchen","dish/woodberry-kitchen"]]}]},"ingredient/maltose":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/maltose","n":"Maltose","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Maltose ( or ), also known as maltobiose or malt sugar, is a disaccharide formed from two units of glucose joined with an α(1→4) bond. In the isomer isomaltose, the two glucose molecules are joined with an α(1→6) bond. Maltose is the two-unit member of the amylose homologous series, the key structural motif of starch. When beta-amylase breaks down starch, it removes two glucose units at a time, producing maltose. An example of this reaction is found in germinating seeds, which is why it was named after malt. Unlike sucrose, it is a reducing sugar."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-maltose"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maltose"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Cantonese cuisine","cuisine/cantonese-cuisine",[["Char siu","dish/char-siu"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Dark soy sauce","ingredient/dark-soy-sauce"],["Fermented bean curd","ingredient/fermented-bean-curd"],["Five-spice powder","ingredient/five-spice-powder"],["Fortified wine","ingredient/fortified-wine"],["Hoisin sauce","ingredient/hoisin-sauce"],["Honey","ingredient/honey"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Rice wine","ingredient/rice-wine"]]}]},"ingredient/hard-boiled-egg":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/hard-boiled-egg","n":"Hard-boiled egg","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 3 cuisines","intro":[["Boiled eggs are a food typically made using chicken eggs. They are cooked with their shells unbroken, usually by immersion in boiling water. Hard-boiled or hard-cooked eggs are cooked so that the egg white and egg yolk both solidify, while soft-boiled eggs may leave the yolk, and sometimes the white, at least partially liquid. Boiled eggs are a popular breakfast food around the world."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-hard-boiled-egg"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hard-boiled_egg"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Pickled egg","dish/pickled-egg"]]],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",[["Pickled egg","dish/pickled-egg"]]],["Western American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states",[["Crab Louie","dish/crab-louie"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Asparagus","ingredient/asparagus"],["Crab meat","ingredient/crab-meat"],["Iceberg lettuce","ingredient/iceberg-lettuce"],["Louis dressing","ingredient/louis-dressing"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Brine","ingredient/brine"],["Curing (food preservation)","ingredient/curing-food-preservation"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Vinegar","ingredient/vinegar"]]}]},"dish/crown-shy":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/crown-shy","n":"Crown Shy","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Crown Shy is a restaurant in New York City, New York in the Financial District. It is located on the ground floor of 70 Pine Street and is associated with Saga; a 2 star Michelin Star restaurant on the 63rd floor; and OverStory, a cocktail bar on the 64th floor which was ranked as the third best bar in the world and the second best in the United States behind Double Chicken Please on The World's 50 Best Bars in 2023. The restaurant serves American cuisine and has received a Michelin star."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-crown-shy"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crown_Shy"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["5-8 Club","dish/5-8-club"],["Altabira City Tavern","dish/altabira-city-tavern"],["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Applebee's","dish/applebee-s"],["Arby's","dish/arby-s"],["Arnold's Bar and Grill","dish/arnold-s-bar-and-grill"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Be Our Guest Restaurant","dish/be-our-guest-restaurant"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Ben's Chili Bowl","dish/ben-s-chili-bowl"],["Benjy's","dish/benjy-s"],["Besaw's","dish/besaw-s"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blackhawk (restaurant)","dish/blackhawk-restaurant"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Bobcat Bite","dish/bobcat-bite"],["Boiling Springs Tavern","dish/boiling-springs-tavern"],["Brix Tavern","dish/brix-tavern"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brown Derby","dish/brown-derby"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Buona","dish/buona"],["Busboys and Poets","dish/busboys-and-poets"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Byways Cafe","dish/byways-cafe"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["California Grill","dish/california-grill"],["Camp Washington Chili","dish/camp-washington-chili"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Carnation Cafe","dish/carnation-cafe"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"]]}]},"dish/feenie-s":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/feenie-s","n":"Feenie's","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Feenie's was a bistro on West Broadway in the Kitsilano neighbourhood of Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada. It was the casual-dining sister-restaurant to Lumière, which was located next-door. Feenie's was founded by celebrity chef Rob Feenie, the first Canadian to win on Iron Chef America. Feenie was co-owner and executive chef until 2007, when he left the restaurant after a falling out with his business partners. After entering into a partnership with chef Daniel Boulud, the majority owners renamed the restaurant \"db Bistro Moderne\". On March 13, 2011, the ownership closed both db Bistro Moderne and Lumière."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-feenie-s"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia